{"id": "17:31", "severity": "minor", "issues": [{"latin": "Deus meus, impollúta via ejus", "portuguese": "Imaculado é o caminho do meu Deus", "problem": "The Latin keeps 'Deus meus' as a hanging nominative/vocative with a resumptive 'ejus'; folding it into a genitive removes the address. Also 'impolluta' (unstained) is rendered with the same word the translation uses for 'immaculatus' in 17:24 and 17:33, blurring a distinction the Latin makes.", "fix": "Meu Deus, sem mancha é o seu caminho, †"}]},
